The [[☃ definition 2]] will pass through points $(0,g(0))$ and $(2,g(2))$.

$\begin{align}
\text{slope}&=\dfrac{\text{change in }y}{\text{change in }x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{g(2)-g(0)}{2-0}
\end{align}$

![Function g is graphed. The x-axis goes from negative 1 to 2.5. The graph consists of a curve. The curve starts in quadrant 2, moves upward with increasing steepness through points (0, g of 0) and (2, g of 2), and ends in quadrant 1. A secant line connects the 2 points.](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/a71da22610391685dc8de47b972bbc9fccc91be4)

We will need to know the values of $g(0)$ and $g(2)$ to find the slope.

$\begin{align}
g(0)&=3^{2(0)}
\\\\
&=1
\\\\
g(2)&=3^{2(2)}
\\\\
&=81
\end{align}$

Now we can find the slope:

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{g(2)-g(0)}{2-0}&=\dfrac{81-1}{2}
\\\\
&=40
\end{align}$
